**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** One entry from an item's model to its bound element, the door S8.2's slots and S11.2's forward model call (001 §N 'One item-model evaluator, ItemModel × parameters × orientation × λ → MuellerMatrix'; .spec-md §3.14: an item instantiates a model, the presets and the stack `Sample` being models themselves). In `ItemEvaluation.fs`, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.1: `ItemEvaluationError` gains `NotAnOpticalElementErr of reason : string`, rendered `the model is not an optical element: <reason>`. `type ItemModelChoice with member this.boundWith (materials : MaterialProxy) (values : ParameterValues) : Result<BoundOpticalElement, ItemEvaluationError>` over step 216's choices: `PolarizerPresetChoice (polarizerModel, p)` is `BoundPolarizerPreset p.behavior`; `StackSampleChoice (sampleModel, _, sample)` is `BoundOpticalElement.ofStackSample materials values sample` (step 249); `LibraryModelChoice v` matches `v.entry.model` (step 208): `OpticalElementModel form` is `BoundOpticalElement.ofOpticalForm values form` (step 248) and `EmptySlotModel` is `BoundEmptySlot`; `IntensityDetectorModel`, `MuellerPolarimeterModel` and `EllipsometerModel` answer `NotAnOpticalElementErr` naming the model, because a detector reads and its gain, dark offset and noise belong to S11.2's forward model; `SourcePresetChoice` answers `NotAnOpticalElementErr` too, a source emitting through `emissionWith` (step 246). No wildcard arm is written, so a later `ItemModelForm` case is a compile error here. No other member is added. Tests, in `ItemEvaluationTests`, with materials from `BuiltinCatalogue.materialStore (fun _ -> [])`: `every item model binds as its kind, and a source or a detector is no optical element`: the `PresetIds.polarizerLp` polarizer binds to its `BoundPolarizerPreset`; `StackSampleChoice` of `SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId` at version 1 evaluates as `ofStackSample` of that sample; the item models of `ItemModelIds.circularPolarizerModelId` and `ItemModelIds.emptySlotModelId` (`BuiltinCatalogue.itemModel`, step 210) over their defaults evaluate as `ofOpticalForm` of their forms and as the identity; and `ItemModelIds.intensityDetectorModelId`, `muellerPolarimeterModelId`, `ellipsometerModelId` and a `SourcePresetChoice` of `PresetIds.heNe633` answer `NotAnOpticalElementErr`. `an item's own parameter values reach its Mueller matrix`: a CPL1 item made by step 216's `ItemDraft` over `LibraryModelChoice (BuiltinCatalogue.itemModel ItemModelIds.circularPolarizerModelId)` and `FixedMounting`, with `c2.retardance` set by `withParameterState` (step 234) to `KnownParameter` π / 4, bound over `ParameterValues.ofParameters item.parameters`, evaluates at 0° to `retarderMueller (45°) (π / 4) · analyzerMueller IdealLinear (0°)` within 1e-12, and its defaults to the quarter-wave product. `every evaluation error renders its condition and its payload` covers `NotAnOpticalElementErr`. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved. LibraryModelChoice of SourcePresetItemModel, IdealPolarizerItemModel or StackSampleItemModel MUST return the typed missing-binding error. Their valid bound choice cases MUST continue calling the same source, polarizer and sample evaluators; no second physics implementation is allowed.

**Acceptance.** After the entry lands, `ItemModelChoice.boundWith` MUST bind every optical model as its kind and answer `NotAnOpticalElementErr` for a detector or a source, and an item's own parameter values MUST reach its Mueller matrix; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `every item model binds as its kind, and a source or a detector is no optical element`, `an item's own parameter values reach its Mueller matrix` and the widened `every evaluation error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the fourteen s25 invariants MUST pass.
